=== 10.2.7: Fuzzy RD (Imperfect Compliance) ===

--- First stage: jump in take-up at cutoff ---
   FS jump  =  0.5783   SE =  0.0454   p(robust) = 0.0000
   h* =  0.302
   Strong first stage: cutoff strongly predicts scholarship take-up.

--- Reduced forms: cutoff → outcome (ITT) ---
   Outcome                 ITT   SE(conv)  p(robust)       h*
   ------------------------------------------------------------ 
   persist_fuzzy        0.0397     0.0540     0.5082    0.225
   credits_y1           5.4000     0.6262     0.0000    0.213
   cgpa_y1              0.0833     0.0518     0.2723    0.194
   ------------------------------------------------------------ 
   ITT: local average effect of eligibility (not take-up) on outcome.

--- Fuzzy LATE (rdrobust, fuzzy option) ---
   Outcome                LATE   SE(conv)  p(robust)       h*
   ------------------------------------------------------------ 
   persist_fuzzy        0.0736     0.0793     0.4790    0.326
   credits_y1           9.1107     1.1685     0.0000    0.270
   cgpa_y1              0.1961     0.0729     0.0240    0.336
   ------------------------------------------------------------ 
   LATE: causal effect for compliers at the cutoff.
   Compliers are a LATENT group: the first stage identifies their share
   at the margin, not which students belong to it.  For credits_y1 and
   cgpa_y1 the exclusion restriction fails by construction; read those
   as Wald arithmetic, not a complier effect.
   Robust CIs: Calonico, Cattaneo & Titiunik (2014, Econometrica).
   h* selected by CCT MSERD criterion separately for each outcome.

--- Covariate-adjusted Fuzzy LATE (rdrobust, covs) ---
   Covariates: female firstgen urm act_score income_cat
   Outcome                LATE   SE(conv)  p(robust)       h*
   ------------------------------------------------------------ 
   persist_fuzzy        0.0701     0.0781     0.5015    0.334
   credits_y1           9.0392     1.1354     0.0000    0.281
   cgpa_y1              0.1974     0.0717     0.0212    0.347
   ------------------------------------------------------------ 
   Wald estimator = RF / FS; covs() reduces outcome residual variance.
   Point estimates stable relative to unadjusted fuzzy LATE above.

